  "lineage": "Norteño repertoire and performance style of the Mexican state of Chihuahua and its Ojinaga-Presidio border corridor, running from the polka, redova and chotis dance forms brought by 19th-century German and Czech settlers through the 1990s romantic-norteño boom codified by Conjunto Primavera and Los Rieleros del Norte — diatonic button accordion carrying the melody in thirds over bajo sexto bass-and-chord strumming, 2/4 polka or 3/4 vals at 110-150 BPM, tololoche or electric bass on the downbeat, and paired baritone-tenor vocal harmony on corridos and romantic canciones.",
